   "<template class=\"ui-dialog-head\"><span class=\"ui-head-name\">demo</span><span class=\"ui-head-where\">App · lab</span></template>\n      <div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><b>Something else applies this app</b><div class=\"ui-callout-body\"><p>Marked as updated by Flux. A change made here can be undone there. To keep it, change it there too.</p><p>A rename creates the app with its new name and removes the old one. Flux then restores the old one, so there are two copies.</p><label class=\"switch\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"editManagedConfirm\"> Flux will bring back the old name</label></div></div>\n    </div>\n      \n      \n      \n      <p><b>demo</b> → <b>demo2</b></p><p>Only the app name changes. Save other changes separately. There is a short outage. Volumes and network addresses are kept.</p>\n      <div class=\"ui-callout info\" role=\"note\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-info\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><div class=\"ui-callout-body\">If a step fails, check both app names in Recent jobs. Homestead does not restart the old copy or remove the new one automatically.</div></div>\n    </div>\n        <details ><summary>Capacity and placement · 1 warning</summary><div class=\"deploy-capacity ui-stack\">\n    <div class=\"capacity-placement\"><section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Host</h4></header>\n    <b>Host not determined</b><p class=\"ui-help\">This review has not confirmed any suitable host.</p></section></div>\n    <section class=\"ui-section\">\n    <header><h4>Placement and memory</h4></header>\n    <div class=\"ui-callout warn\" role=\"alert\">\n      <span class=\"ui-callout-icon\"><svg class=\"ui-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-alert\"/></svg></span>\n      <div><div class=\"ui-notice-line ui-notice-whole\"><b class=\"ui-notice-head\">Check the placement and memory.</b><span class=\"ui-notice-first ui-issue-short\">unknown &lt;memory&gt;</span></div></div>\n    </div></section>\n    <details class=\"ui-more\" data-disclosure=\"How this is estimated\">\n    <summary>How this is estimated</summary><div class=\"ui-more-body\">\n      \n      <p>Capacity warnings, such as high expected memory use or missing usage figures, can be accepted. Continuing may cause memory shortages, restarts or downtime. It does not change the reserved resources or limits.</p>\n      <p>This is a snapshot. It does not reserve capacity or guarantee that memory is sufficient. Homestead checks again before creating anything. The planned volumes have not been created yet.</p></div></details>\n    \n  </div></details>\n      \n      <label class=\"switch\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"editCapacityConfirm\"> Rename it despite the outage</label>\n      <div class=\"ui-actions\" >\n      <div class=\"ui-actions-start\"><button data-dialog-dismiss=\"true\" class=\"btn\" onclick=\"modalBack()\">Back to edit</button></div><div class=\"ui-actions-end\"><button id=\"editGo\" class=\"btn pri\"  onclick=\"confirmEdit()\">Rename app</button></div></div>"
